    narr:generatedFrom "08dbf2d09d3a625ffd65c009778ee0a98c8715fd" ;
    narr:narration """This narrative opens with the interview-flywheel motion: [one expert conversation producing three outputs — installable perspective, published content, live demo](narr:Expr_1RealFreyaPodcastSalesMotion20260323_4), framed as [a content flywheel that also builds marketplace supply](narr:Expr_1RealFreyaPodcastSalesMotion20260323_5), with [the breakthrough that demo call, marketing content, and onboarding are the same event](narr:Expr_1RealFreyaPodcastSalesMotion20260323_3). Its origin runs through [casual musing about packaging interviews as installable expertise](narr:Expr_1RealFreyaPodcastSalesMotion20260323_7) and [seeding first modules with expertise from people she knows](narr:Expr_1RealFreyaPodcastSalesMotion20260323_34), instantiated in [Freya wanting to interview himself into an installable design-approach perspective](narr:Expr_1RealFreyaPodcastSalesMotion20260323_37) as [one of the first marketplace perspectives](narr:Expr_1RealFreyaPodcastSalesMotion20260323_38), with [his grasp of how the interview removes the expert's setup barrier](narr:Expr_1RealFreyaPodcastSalesMotion20260323_41). Execution details include [hosting/subdomain plans where the published version should feel like a media property](narr:Expr_1RealFreyaPodcastSalesMotion20260323_44) and [outreach templates committing to explicit free-vs-paid terms, no bait and switch](narr:Expr_1RealFreyaPodcastSalesMotion20260323_45). A second thread grew alongside: [the challenge that texting carries a spam-trained trust cost in skeptical contexts](narr:Expr_2RealTessChatWidget20260423_9), grounded in [seven rejected toll-free numbers](narr:Expr_2RealTessChatWidget20260423_14), answered by [a chat widget on the share page for evaluator and demo contexts](narr:Expr_2RealTessChatWidget20260423_30) with [one widget per share ID architecture](narr:Expr_2RealTessChatWidget20260423_22) and [a Front widget spike to test automation](narr:Expr_2RealTessChatWidget20260423_68). A third turn reframes the whole question as [channel-not-product: right in some contexts, wrong in others](narr:Expr_3RealChannelNotProduct20260428_14), holding that [the phone number's non-AI texture is real value](narr:Expr_3RealChannelNotProduct20260428_15) and that [the SMS-honesty claim is not superseded](narr:Expr_3RealChannelNotProduct20260428_17), while [a second seven-number rejection cycle](narr:Expr_3RealChannelNotProduct20260428_22) established [verification churn as a permanent operational cost](narr:Expr_3RealChannelNotProduct20260428_25). Two position nodes carry the open questions: [how channel selection shapes trust across high-trust versus skeptical evaluator contexts](narr:Position_EvaluatorChannelTrustTax) and [how per-share chat surfaces should be provisioned without founder triage](narr:Position_PerShareChatWidgetArchitecture).""" ;
